 ## Overview
-Quilez Ambient Occlusion is a fast approximation for ambient occlusion in Signed Distance Field (SDF) rendering that estimates surface visibility by ray marching along the surface normal [S1, S3, unofficial]. Unlike Evans Ambient Occlusion, which measures the difference between the sampled distance and the distance field value at a single point, Quilez's method accumulates occlusion contributions from multiple samples along the normal, weighting closer geometry more heavily [S3, unofficial]. It differs from standard ray marching by using no explicit intersection checks and marching along the normal instead of a hemisphere [S4, unofficial].
